# Generated/vendored audio assets, not source. `format`'s glob is `.` (the
# whole repo), and prettier has no idea `-mp3.js` files carry a strict data
# contract (`"B1": "data:..."`, double-quoted keys) that `parseSamplePack`
# requires — its own style (singleQuote, unquoted-where-valid keys) silently
# breaks it into `B1: 'data:...'`, which parses to zero samples. That is
# exactly how the percussion packs shipped broken for months: nothing threw,
# nothing failed a typecheck, the only symptom was drums with no sound. See
# music_app_rn's src/config/soundfont-assets.test.ts, which is what caught it.
public/audio/
